  "verdict": "For the open torch-free HGB analogue, adding docking / RMT-RTE does NOT improve confidence in either regime. (1) As features: the 217 RDKit-2D descriptors already saturate \u2014 Brier/ECE/AUC are flat-to-worse on random splits and on the scaffold split (structure AUC is the best rung in both). (2) As the p_QSAR x p_RMT-RTE veto: the precision@0.7 / FPR gains are a thresholding artifact \u2014 coverage collapses (0.45->0.18 random) while ranking degrades (AUC 0.918->0.901); at matched coverage the structure model alone is more precise (0.987 vs veto 0.952), and symmetric mean-fusion is no better. The scaffold split repeats this (structure matched-cov precision 0.772 vs veto 0.697). RMT-RTE is a weak (~0.80 AUC) standalone signal that only dilutes the strong structure model. Where RMT genuinely helps is the DMPNN/blend (see dmpnn_blend_reference), not this analogue: the paper's confidence gain lives in the graph net."
}